    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 2004, a four-year-old boy named Aristo Sham played Mozart’s music at the Shanghai Concert Hall, earning him the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "nickname",
            "ref": "v-nickname"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " “Little Mozart”. Now 21 years have passed, and he is back again—but this time, as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "world champion",
            "zh": "世界冠军"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " pianist!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "The Van Cliburn International Piano Competition",
            "zh": "范·克莱本国际钢琴比赛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is like the “World Cup” of piano. In 2025, 29-year-old Aristo won first prize. He is now only the second Chinese pianist to achieve this."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Aristo said the timing was just right. “If I had won earlier, I might not have been ready,” he said. “Now I understand music more deeply, and I know what I want to do next. Patience turned out to be a good thing!”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Aristo started his music journey early. At the age of 10, he won a prize in an international contest in Germany. Like Lang Lang, who also gained early recognition in international contests. People called Aristo a "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "child prodigy",
            "ref": "v-child-prodigy"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But he said that name sometimes felt heavy. “People still remember me as a kid,” he said. “But I hope they see who I am now.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Unlike what many people think, Aristo never practised all day. He plays the piano for no more than four hours a day. “The key is to stay 100% "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "focused",
            "ref": "v-focused"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ",” he said. “You should make the best use of every minute.” Aristo believes that rest is also very important. Sometimes, he even takes two weeks off to let his mind and body fully relax."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On November 8, 2025, Aristo returned to the Shanghai Concert Hall for his first show after winning the Van Cliburn "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "competition",
            "ref": "v-competition"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". He played his winning piece and brought us some truly wonderful music."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
